# Keyboard.onKey / onChar are private — widened so VirtualKeyboard can route synthetic typing through
# the real methods instead of calling Screen.keyPressed/charTyped directly. Mods built on Architectury
# API (e.g. Roughly Enough Items) intercept input via @WrapOperation mixins on the Screen.mouseClicked/
# keyPressed/charTyped CALL SITES inside Mouse.onMouseButton/Keyboard.onKey/onChar — a direct call to
# the Screen method from elsewhere in the codebase never reaches those call sites, so those mods never
# see synthetic input from the virtual mouse/keyboard. Routing through the real methods fixes that for
# REI and any other Architectury-based mod, not just REI specifically (feedback: "no es integrarlo, es
# interactuar con el").
accessible method net/minecraft/client/Keyboard onKey (JILnet/minecraft/client/input/KeyInput;)V
accessible method net/minecraft/client/Keyboard onChar (JLnet/minecraft/client/input/CharInput;)V
